The expression grammar will be very similar to Lox.
How it works is that an expression can be a binary, a unary, a grouping, or a literal.
A binary will have the format of expression, operator, expression.
A unary will have the format of operator, expression.
A grouping will have the format of expression inside parenthasis.
A literal will be a value, number, string, boolean, or NULL.

There is no special set up for the ast printer other than having access to the main python program
containing Language and a .language file containing hard coded asts.
Entering an ast after accessing the main python program with the command line also works.

All test cases were tested with the file and typed with REPL and all worked and are written in Lab2test1.

test 1:
This was testing having it start with a Grouping and testing the Binary with literals and
the PLUS token.
Hard Coded ast:
    Grouping(Binary(Literal(1), Token(TokenType.PLUS, "+", None, 1), Literal(2)))
expected output: Structure: (group (+ 1 2))
actual output: Structure: (group (+ 1 2))
This matched the expected result.

test 2:
This was testing having it start with Binary with nested Unary and Grouping as well 
as the ASTRIX and MINUS tokens.
Hard Coded ast:
    Binary(Unary(Token(TokenType.MINUS, "-", None, 1),Literal(123)), Token(TokenType.ASTRIX,"*", None, 1), Grouping(Literal(45.67)))
expected output: Structure: (* (- 123) (group 45.67))
actual output: Structure: (* (- 123) (group 45.67))
This matched the expected result.

test 3:
This was testing having it start with Unary having a nested Grouping with a nested Binary
as well as the SLASH token.
Hard Coded ast:
    Unary(Token(TokenType.MINUS, "-", None, 1),Grouping(Binary(Literal(12),Token(TokenType.SLASH,"/", None, 1), Literal(34))))
expected output: Structure: (- (group (/ 12 34)))
actual output: Structure: (- (group (/ 12 34)))
This matched the expected result.

test 4:
This was testing running the file with multiple ast and having it print each one seperate.
Hard Coded ast:
    Grouping(Binary(Literal(1), Token(TokenType.PLUS, "+", None, 1), Literal(2)))

    Binary(Unary(Token(TokenType.MINUS, "-", None, 3),Literal(123)), Token(TokenType.ASTRIX,"*", None, 3), Grouping(Literal(45.67)))

    Unary(Token(TokenType.MINUS, "-", None, 5),Grouping(Binary(Literal(12),Token(TokenType.SLASH,"/", None, 5), Literal(34))))
expected result:
    Structure: (group (+ 1 2))
    Structure: (* (- 123) (group 45.67))
    Structure: (- (group (/ 12 34)))
actual result:
    Structure: (group (+ 1 2))
    Structure: (* (- 123) (group 45.67))
    Structure: (- (group (/ 12 34)))
This matched the expected result.

Limitations:
The limitations are that the hard coded ast in the file being read must be done in a single
line. This can make it harder to be sure the ast is written properly.
